ample: find doubled words**\n\n```regex\n\\b(\\w+)\\s+\\1\\b\n```\n\n- `(\\w+)` captures a word, e.g. `the`\n- `\\s+` matches the whitespace after it\n- `\\1` requires the exact same text `the` to appear again\n\nSo in `\"I saw the the cat\"`, it matches `the the`. It does not match `\"the cat\"`, because `\\1` would need `the` and finds `cat`.\n\nCompare this with `(\\w+)\\s+\\w+`, which would match any two words. The backreference is what forces the two to be identical.","ttft_ms":3854,"type":"result","duration_ms":3880,"uuid":"aac4928e-a272-4578-a0ba-a4e60b6e1dfb","ttft_stream_ms":971,"time_to_request_ms":208,"first_content_frame_ms":971,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":307,"cacheReadInputTokens":2980,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006744,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}